- `action(n1, "start the process")`: Omits the explicit scheduling constraint stated in the source: "start the process at 8:00 am". (SMC2)
- `action(n13, "every wednesday evening: take books to miranda")`: Payload is incomplete relative to the source text: "take the letter book and member register to Miranda". (SMC2)
- `action(n14, "applicant becomes member")` & `action(n23, "applicant cannot become member")`: Incorrectly modeled as executable task steps rather than decision outcomes; the source presents these as conditional branches ("If the applicant becomes a member... If the applicant cannot become a member..."). (SMC2, SMC4)
- `branch(b5, XOR)` & `branch(b6, XOR)`: Declared as exclusive-choice gateways but each possesses only a single outgoing precedence edge (`n15` and `n24` respectively), violating XOR control-flow semantics which require at least two mutually exclusive paths. (SMC4)
- `guard(b5, n15, v5 = 'Yes')`: Attached to a branch with only one outgoing path, rendering the guard logically inert and failing to route or evaluate the rejection scenario. (SMC4, SMC5)
- `defines(v4, ..., {})`, `defines(v5, ..., {"Yes"})`, `defines(v6, ..., {})`: Contain empty or incomplete value ranges, failing to define valid evaluation spaces for their respective conditions. (SMC6)
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Assigns every process node to a single generic actor, completely ignoring explicit participant responsibilities for "Miranda" (receiving books) and "Charles" (handling letters, updating registers) detailed in the description. (SMC7)

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b5` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b6` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b5,XOR); branch(b6,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v4` has an invalid range `[]`. | Variable `v5` has an invalid range `['Yes']`. | Variable `v6` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v5 = 'Yes'` on `b5 -> n15` uses undefined variable `v5`. | DSL: guard(b5,n15,"v5 = 'Yes'")
- [S4] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n14` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b4 -> n23` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b6 -> n24` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v5 = 'Yes'` on `b5 -> n15` cannot be evaluated: `v5` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b5,n15,"v5 = 'Yes'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b5` cannot be evaluated: `v5` has no declared range.
